@page "/wiki/origins"
@page "/wiki/origins/{Key}"

@*
    The origins, which are the same records as the civics with a flag set and a very different job.

    An origin is the whole of how an empire starts - its homeworld, sometimes a second species, and
    a scene of the world it wakes up on - where a civic is one of two picks. That is why they are
    two pages rather than one list with a switch: a reader looking for an origin is asking a
    different question from one looking for a civic, even though the answer comes out of the same
    three hundred and fifty-eight entries.

    The second address is one entry of the shelf. It shows the same page and picks that one out, so a
    reader who found the thing they came for can send somebody straight to it rather than to a list
    with an instruction to scroll.
*@

<PageTitle>Origins - Stellaris Empire Manager</PageTitle>

<WikiSection Kind="WikiKind.Origins" Focus="@Key" />

@code {
    /// <summary>The entry the address names, where it names one.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? Key { get; set; }
}
